# Exocortex — Master Plan

**Status:** Round 2 review open. `round-2-review.prd` is the current
worklist (B3-B7, W9-W14, H9-H14, P1). Round-1 closure verified by audit:
14/19 items fully closed with tests; W7/H1/H2/H6 carry residue (H12).

**Process blocker (P1):** the round-1 closure exists only as uncommitted
working-tree changes — commit it before round-2 work starts.

**Purpose:** The authoritative, phased worklist for this repository. Each
round of review findings gets its own `round-<n>-review.prd`; accepted
items are promoted into this file, tracked to done, and never silently
dropped. Anything not listed here is either shipped or explicitly deferred
to v2 in the PRD's own terms.

**Current baseline (re-verified 2026-08-23, round 2):** 106 tests,
0 failed; clippy/fmt/deny green; kernel-purity, fingerprint
(`d8bcd004…4e8c`, stable), no-llm, and both SLO bench gates green
(search p99 drifted 680→731µs, still inside the 3ms budget). Full detail:
`round-2-review.prd`.

**Known caveat:** no CI pipeline exists — all gates are manual `cargo xtask`
invocations (round-2 item W10).

## Initial build (M0–M8, shipped 2026-08)

All nine milestones landed in order, one commit each, every gate green at
each step (88 tests at completion).

| Milestone | Delivered |
|---|---|
| M0 | Workspace scaffolding: kernel, wire, xtask; toolchain/dep pins resolved (deviations recorded in `MILESTONE_REPORT.md`) |
| M1 | Ontology: `pack!` macro engine, dev-v1 pack (13 memory types, 12 entity types, 48 kinds), R-Pk/R-T validators |
| M2 | Storage: `Storage` trait, registered Cypher catalogue, FalkorDB adapter, InMemory double, bi-temporal reads |
| M3 | Cache + MCP client: ArcSwap snapshots, 2Q admission, sled WAL, stdio MCP server, search SLO bench (100k) |
| M4 | Reasoning: Crepe R1–R9 + D1–D6 fixpoints, Steel explain traces + R6, idempotent derived-edge writeback |
| M5 | Cluster: owner leases with epoch fencing, HMAC-signed envelopes, peer admission, SSE change feed |
| M6 | Ingestion: IngestService pipeline (HMAC → fingerprint → ceiling → triples), entity extraction, `end_session` tool, worker host |
| M7 | Operation registry: one entry per operation, MCP+HTTP schema parity, audit ledger, goldens |
| M8 | Dreams: MCR² + sparsity guardrails, consolidation cycle with rollback, trigger model, discovery proposals |

